onstitutional symptoms but lacks localized neurological deficits", "Diabetic complication syndrome: Visual changes could relate to diabetes but inconsistent with acute pancytopenia"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B symptoms (weight loss, night sweats, fever)", "Acute-onset neurological deficits (headache, visual acuity changes)", "Pancytopenia with blasts"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.35302715766484416, "posterior": 0.3687453942791943, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute presentation with constitutional symptoms and blasts is more consistent with AML than chronic myeloproliferative disorders."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of skin findings (e.g., petechiae, ecchymoses) slightly favors lymphoid over myeloid blast proliferation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urgency"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.161, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Acute neurological symptoms moderately favor myeloid over lymphoid processes but do not confirm a specific subtype."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.015, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Acute neurological symptoms are more typical of myeloid blast crises than lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorders."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.08340292289856699, "posterior": 0.06274365298141225, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Acute neurological symptoms are more typical of myeloid blast crises than lymphoproliferative/plasma cell disorders."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B4.1", "B4.2", "B4.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.01, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3244187980485683, "posterior": 0.34116721004564016, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["The subacute symptoms and blasts moderately favor AML over chronic myeloid processes but provide only weak_for evidence compared to lymphoid neoplasms due to t…"], "evidence_against": ["Lack of skin findings moderately supports lymphoid neoplasms over de novo AML but is not definitive."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.013, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Subacute presentation with acute symptoms strongly excludes CML-BC, which typically has a chronic course."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.015, "danger": 0.7,