 than lymphoid blast proliferation, thus contradicting the lymphoid neoplasm hypothesis?", "summary": "Acute neurological findings weakly favor myeloid processes but do not definitively exclude lymphoid neoplasms, which can present with atypical manifestations."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the absence of bone pain or gum bleeding (common in ALL) a strong argument against de novo ALL as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Absence of typical ALL physical findings weakly reduces its likelihood but does not exclude it due to variability in clinical presentation."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset over days with constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) and the presence of blasts in peripheral blood strongly support the diagnosis of de novo AML compared to other myel…", "summary": "The subacute symptoms and blasts moderately favor AML over chronic myeloid processes but provide only weak_for evidence compared to lymphoid neoplasms due to the lack of definitive myeloid-specific features."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of typical AML features such as skin manifestations (e.g., petechiae, ecchymoses) suggest that the high blast count may not be due to de novo AML but rather a lymphoid neoplasm or an…", "summary": "The absence of skin findings weakly reduces the likelihood of de novo AML but does not eliminate it, as these features can be variable. This provides neutral evidence for AML and weak_for for MDS/therapy-related AML."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.393], ["B4", 0.374], ["B1.1", 0.275]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.274], ["B1.1", 0.237], ["B4", 0.187]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.353], ["B1.1", 0.324], ["B2", 0.184]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers (airway, respiratory, or circulatory compromise) are present. Time-critical syndromes (stroke, septic shock, tension pneumothorax) are not supported by clinical findings.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "working_differential", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1.1: AML) posterior (0.324) remains <0.75, and dangerous unresolved alternatives (B2: Lymphoid Neoplasm with posterior 0.184, danger 0.85) exist. Further testing required to distinguish myeloid vs lymphoid lineage."}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 1.05, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.3244187980485683, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'bleeding', 'visual changes', 'gum bleeding', 'bone pain', 'petechiae', 'ecchymoses', 'ataxia', 'neoplasm', 'Bruising susceptibility'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.393}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "posterior": 0.341, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 5, "disconfirming": 2, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Lack of skin findings moderately supports lymphoid neoplasms over de novo AML but is not definitive."}, "action_intents": [{"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B2